      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_02097bcea6698d3843094196e6a30b0da38d2e2ecaa79666d674640d0b92f9e9",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Subtracting the value and tangent of the inverse-square interaction at normalized gap one produces a convex nonnegative defect V. Pairwise it vanishes when the absolute normalized gap equals one—not uniquely at the unshifted reference configuration—and interval summation cancels the linear displacement term up to polylogarithmic boundary error. The span then states the stronger integrated-energy target and introduces a smooth weight ψ_T to localize a globally weighted renormalized energy.",
