    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5819c5a4e3bae8d8979c2196fcffd26403712ff3dffe840abadac7036e5b8268",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Finite-index truncation first turns the zero ODE into legal identities and exposes interactions with the complement as environmental error terms. A pigeonholed cutoff bounds that leakage and supplies weak integrated energy sufficient for later interchange of time integration and infinite summation. Subtracting the value and tangent of the inverse-square and logarithmic interactions at the classical-location gap, then applying a decaying spatial weight, produces nonnegative localized defects; multiscale decay, symmetrization, and cancellation against the classical reference finally yield an absolutely continuous Hamiltonian with derivative -4 times the renormalized energy up to negligible error. This chain converts the formal infinite gradient flow into a rigorous scale-local equilibrium detector whose pair defects vanish at the corresponding classical spacing.",
